# ColorFit Frontend Rules

## Technology

- Use React with TypeScript.
- Use React Router for routing.
- Use Tailwind CSS for styling.
- Use GSAP for complex animations.
- Prefer CSS/Tailwind transitions for simple animations.

## Components

- Keep components focused on a single responsibility.
- Reuse existing components before creating new ones.
- Do not create duplicate UI components.
- Separate Page Components, Feature Components, and reusable UI Components.

## Routing

- Follow the routes defined in `docs/screen-list.md`.
- Do not add or change routes without updating the relevant documentation.

## API

- API communication must be separated from UI components.
- Do not put HTTP request logic directly into presentation components.
- Follow `docs/06_api.md` for API contracts.

## State

- Prefer local React state when possible.
- Use custom hooks when state or logic becomes complex.
- Do not introduce a global state library unless there is a clear requirement.

## Styling

- Use Tailwind CSS according to `docs/08_ui_guideline.md`.
- Do not introduce arbitrary styling that conflicts with the existing design system.
- Follow the UI references under `docs/ui-reference/`.

## Responsive

- All screens must support mobile, tablet, and desktop layouts.
- Do not implement desktop-only layouts.

## Accessibility

- Use semantic HTML where appropriate.
- Form controls must have accessible labels.
- Interactive elements must be keyboard accessible.
- Do not rely on color alone to communicate important information.

## Image Processing

- Do not implement core image processing logic in the frontend.
- Image processing must be handled by the Python backend.
